[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-35994"] :question/problem "Find $f(x,y)$ such that $∇f=F,$ where $F(x,y)=-y\\,i+(3-x)\\,j.$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y)=F(x,y),$ the function $f(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=3-x\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (-y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-xy+g(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-x+{g}^{′}(y).\n$$\n\nTaking  $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=3-x$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x+{g}^{′}(y) & =3-x \\\\ {g}^{′}(y) & =3 \\\\ g(y) & =3y+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nFinally, substituting $g(y)=3y+C$ into our expression for $f(x,y),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=-xy+3y+C.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-132079/selection/bf5eb5d7242d4c5ed93003eb99e34490b8b6035ccacd58c7a4c4792e3a318548" :answer/id #uuid "7caad36c-4446-5829-8909-f200751dffd2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)=y{e}^{y}+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132079/selection/5abdeacd0b3cd5e7c534cc3f2590f841f897da18df28e892bd8670c11c477dc5" :answer/id #uuid "d77c35b4-4f94-5533-a1b1-198ce67c5128" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)=x{e}^{y}+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132079/selection/75c8384d716abfb93319a825db54e0e32454f781fb791617f7a3cc4dc31a4833" :answer/id #uuid "9676dda2-5870-5cfb-96ca-819fad85e341" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)=x{e}^{y}+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132079/selection/2d79e64642b1f2d42da3fbc0e3abff1770d0ce5303a6ffa0fb65ec47b5b41cad" :answer/id #uuid "58945b57-636e-5531-b88b-26eb2eb48d30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)={y}^{2}{e}^{y}+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132079/selection/c8043c465289e3a1a2217cd1611f3d9ea76c48045b6f8dd7ff993abe91c59435" :answer/id #uuid "6e5af536-28be-5bb3-9611-daf4566032fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)={x}^{2}{e}^{y}+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132079/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fae8dd34-7873-5ef1-b9d6-d8d93bf24cc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132079/selection/5abdeacd0b3cd5e7c534cc3f2590f841f897da18df28e892bd8670c11c477dc5" :answer-field/choices ["q-132079/selection/bf5eb5d7242d4c5ed93003eb99e34490b8b6035ccacd58c7a4c4792e3a318548" "q-132079/selection/5abdeacd0b3cd5e7c534cc3f2590f841f897da18df28e892bd8670c11c477dc5" "q-132079/selection/75c8384d716abfb93319a825db54e0e32454f781fb791617f7a3cc4dc31a4833" "q-132079/selection/2d79e64642b1f2d42da3fbc0e3abff1770d0ce5303a6ffa0fb65ec47b5b41cad" "q-132079/selection/c8043c465289e3a1a2217cd1611f3d9ea76c48045b6f8dd7ff993abe91c59435"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132079" :question/id #uuid "a29ac642-40c5-580f-8da2-e18835fd2a8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-132079" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y)$ such that $∇f=F,$ where $F(x,y)=({e}^{y}-y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,i+(x{e}^{y}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,j.$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y)=F(x,y),$ the function $f(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={e}^{y}-y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{y}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int ({e}^{y}-y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{e}^{y}+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+g(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{y}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{g}^{′}(y).\n$$\n\nTaking  $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{y}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x{e}^{y}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{g}^{′}(y) & =x{e}^{y}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ {g}^{′}(y) & =0 \\\\ g(y) & =C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nFinally, substituting $g(y)=C$ into our expression for $f(x,y),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=x{e}^{y}+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-132079/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97730a2e-3d3e-5a2c-b366-7a3b1eafbe63"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132079"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81734/selection/68bffc253ba143c970c58195da882479192368a79e21b1b0a145c34610e8a32f" :answer/id #uuid "5886feb5-0b19-52cd-b310-9dc9f6836c8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)=4xy+xy+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81734/selection/9a3c4db835a35d092aba03d51cfa24bd04f39de02111c2969aaae19959fdfbc5" :answer/id #uuid "ad1099ca-da5a-539c-adc9-c5bef6a4025d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)=2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81734/selection/3607a12e2d32971a4c4d0af0896d229d411619ede6ddc1974e51f8515d3bac76" :answer/id #uuid "ad8f90dd-8237-511d-8a06-78ae385b0791" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}+x+y+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81734/selection/271684017ecf633584512bb1f10bc2b26816328827d6e52ca19219651ef55967" :answer/id #uuid "c941d96b-e88b-51d6-95db-f32a9b8ea84e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}+y+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81734/selection/53ff780a21c4a66999618931332916797a3bf47f15e1dfb82c08c3791e26cba7" :answer/id #uuid "17dc26f4-c053-5d8e-a780-1498c13f4485" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)=2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81734/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "204adce6-2eca-5810-8392-934b6f601b0b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81734/selection/3607a12e2d32971a4c4d0af0896d229d411619ede6ddc1974e51f8515d3bac76" :answer-field/choices ["q-81734/selection/68bffc253ba143c970c58195da882479192368a79e21b1b0a145c34610e8a32f" "q-81734/selection/9a3c4db835a35d092aba03d51cfa24bd04f39de02111c2969aaae19959fdfbc5" "q-81734/selection/3607a12e2d32971a4c4d0af0896d229d411619ede6ddc1974e51f8515d3bac76" "q-81734/selection/271684017ecf633584512bb1f10bc2b26816328827d6e52ca19219651ef55967" "q-81734/selection/53ff780a21c4a66999618931332916797a3bf47f15e1dfb82c08c3791e26cba7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81734" :question/id #uuid "4f41d6a8-6f93-5f74-922f-5d09a179c65b" :question/math-academy-id "q-81734" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y)$ such that $∇f=F,$ where $F(x,y)=(2x{y}^{2}+1)\\,i+(2{x}^{2}y+1)\\,j.$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y)=F(x,y),$ the function $f(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x{y}^{2}+1,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2{x}^{2}y+1\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2x{y}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}{y}^{2}+x+g(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2{x}^{2}y+{g}^{′}(y).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2{x}^{2}y+1$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}y+{g}^{′}(y) & =2{x}^{2}y+1 \\\\ {g}^{′}(y) & =1 \\\\ g(y) & =y+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nFinally, substituting $g(y)=y+C$ into our expression for $f(x,y),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}+x+y+C.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-81734/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97730a2e-3d3e-5a2c-b366-7a3b1eafbe63"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81734"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132077/selection/34d05aee2f44a2263c4357b02b8cc5244450ab8dc099d16564e6dd467f4ebceb" :answer/id #uuid "05bbffe2-f92b-570c-a819-8681895a20ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}y+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132077/selection/cdbcbe4bd1b385fa3e55d5c63937f9d0fa099e6eb4fd9b65a85b592db378e1bc" :answer/id #uuid "fe401cf1-8bbe-56f9-a418-ebedc8f5748f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)+{y}^{2}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132077/selection/c8f96ec55f653c0077771efd74f388bc269f76a0cc0fc9d846e6bc959f713859" :answer/id #uuid "55accdcc-c5b9-5d25-977c-f2635b9fdd2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)+x+y+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132077/selection/0d819836acb3e38bee0fdcac17794bd15ac1adde44bd0989aa147717e5badf93" :answer/id #uuid "32204b71-af4f-57d4-8085-6de44422b55c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132077/selection/cada36b584cbf8eed23fe53cd8b88fb9e8591cfe27006e5bc62b6958d87dbb05" :answer/id #uuid "75876fc3-127c-5bfa-906c-0153844f8b3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)+xy+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132077/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ed5ee9ad-6605-5b15-97b7-79e7cb030682" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132077/selection/cada36b584cbf8eed23fe53cd8b88fb9e8591cfe27006e5bc62b6958d87dbb05" :answer-field/choices ["q-132077/selection/34d05aee2f44a2263c4357b02b8cc5244450ab8dc099d16564e6dd467f4ebceb" "q-132077/selection/cdbcbe4bd1b385fa3e55d5c63937f9d0fa099e6eb4fd9b65a85b592db378e1bc" "q-132077/selection/c8f96ec55f653c0077771efd74f388bc269f76a0cc0fc9d846e6bc959f713859" "q-132077/selection/0d819836acb3e38bee0fdcac17794bd15ac1adde44bd0989aa147717e5badf93" "q-132077/selection/cada36b584cbf8eed23fe53cd8b88fb9e8591cfe27006e5bc62b6958d87dbb05"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132077" :question/id #uuid "68e41e8c-a69a-5d43-a9b3-91bf34e5d4cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-132077" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y)$ such that $∇f=F,$ where $F(x,y)=(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)+y)\\,i+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)+x)\\,j.$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y)=F(x,y),$ the function $f(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)+y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)+x\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)+y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)+xy+g(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)+x+{g}^{′}(y).\n$$\n\nTaking  $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)+x$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)+x+{g}^{′}(y) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)+x \\\\ {g}^{′}(y) & =0 \\\\ g(y) & =C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nFinally, substituting $g(y)=C$ into our expression for $f(x,y),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)+xy+C.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-132077/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97730a2e-3d3e-5a2c-b366-7a3b1eafbe63"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132077"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81748/selection/ebafe3a0a708db3ed057fdb00852ec3440226823747f6a667d51ed3f23bd0b1c" :answer/id #uuid "d48face2-6388-5853-a259-cd8ae546ed38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)={sin}^{2}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81748/selection/b5c11364e29ef6e0f1df6ef3726c20d020a93b77867aee79b962f27df7efe20c" :answer/id #uuid "57789520-8726-50e7-a2b1-1a3fe7c524b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81748/selection/4fc24c72b9beb88c1a124ea3a750ceba7b27d46ec105670a0ecb07d35f18a6b7" :answer/id #uuid "d7de3ab3-6985-59b6-b7f0-fd14c8c12afc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81748/selection/68ac12c184c328ead4e9aa37b21fa77e3a70eb9faafc389af95975495cd9af0a" :answer/id #uuid "c615c58a-0442-58a1-971a-3e9bc74f35bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81748/selection/ed4d4f3dbd8e77ca3f96f4621f673bf7d4d3316013622ba2937241768c55f27e" :answer/id #uuid "942c3754-860c-5afb-8c7c-bf40b4117c1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81748/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e2cca0b7-71c2-5540-a22e-a01d3718b9f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81748/selection/4fc24c72b9beb88c1a124ea3a750ceba7b27d46ec105670a0ecb07d35f18a6b7" :answer-field/choices ["q-81748/selection/ebafe3a0a708db3ed057fdb00852ec3440226823747f6a667d51ed3f23bd0b1c" "q-81748/selection/b5c11364e29ef6e0f1df6ef3726c20d020a93b77867aee79b962f27df7efe20c" "q-81748/selection/4fc24c72b9beb88c1a124ea3a750ceba7b27d46ec105670a0ecb07d35f18a6b7" "q-81748/selection/68ac12c184c328ead4e9aa37b21fa77e3a70eb9faafc389af95975495cd9af0a" "q-81748/selection/ed4d4f3dbd8e77ca3f96f4621f673bf7d4d3316013622ba2937241768c55f27e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81748" :question/id #uuid "fa1b5396-84b4-5b2e-ab79-d9e21cc54a7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-81748" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y)$ such that $∇f=F,$ where $F(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,i+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\,j.$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y)=F(x,y),$ the function $f(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+g(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+{g}^{′}(y).\n$$\n\nTaking  $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+{g}^{′}(y) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y \\\\ {g}^{′}(y) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡y \\\\ g(y) & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nFinally, substituting $g(y)=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+C$ into our expression for $f(x,y),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+C.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-81748/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97730a2e-3d3e-5a2c-b366-7a3b1eafbe63"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81748"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124729/selection/00514953b5cd60a228e8c2a024173133e1c96ada2655e06e5756d48865aedb92" :answer/id #uuid "850ffa8c-c7b2-550b-98db-3c89c5f951dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}z+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124729/selection/0f11ddaa965b8495a50a191b336ec0123bda6f89ff56bcec94083d7dc8b1ec35" :answer/id #uuid "149ea04e-66f8-5e19-b4d9-259d197a3f4a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}{z}^{2}+{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124729/selection/4f94bb64b65f31ee8c0415aac2204eb4052a8dcfbf6fa0e4d1f94a316c865087" :answer/id #uuid "70a63e5d-bbb0-511f-8c29-b51f3ec807a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xy+{x}^{2}z+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124729/selection/60b4b19438671f58437ebd5270f1ba19392b7248493df1d22123dbbca78c6b52" :answer/id #uuid "051d5421-f4e3-52b3-a545-d88a40476684" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=x{y}^{2}-z\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124729/selection/4d1988db12077a4ec2dd1ffd6f6d648dee03845afc5096b9b313649a39404133" :answer/id #uuid "9cbe9721-a32a-505a-b844-9c3331e21d26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+yz+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124729/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "59f9a68f-8e05-5cc7-80f5-482098347c63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124729/selection/00514953b5cd60a228e8c2a024173133e1c96ada2655e06e5756d48865aedb92" :answer-field/choices ["q-124729/selection/00514953b5cd60a228e8c2a024173133e1c96ada2655e06e5756d48865aedb92" "q-124729/selection/0f11ddaa965b8495a50a191b336ec0123bda6f89ff56bcec94083d7dc8b1ec35" "q-124729/selection/4f94bb64b65f31ee8c0415aac2204eb4052a8dcfbf6fa0e4d1f94a316c865087" "q-124729/selection/60b4b19438671f58437ebd5270f1ba19392b7248493df1d22123dbbca78c6b52" "q-124729/selection/4d1988db12077a4ec2dd1ffd6f6d648dee03845afc5096b9b313649a39404133"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124729" :question/id #uuid "37a4f167-d075-5cc5-b42f-1d28c266ec7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-124729" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ where $F(x,y,z)=(2xz+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\,i+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,j+{x}^{2}\\,k.$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y,z)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\,k.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2xz+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}={x}^{2}\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2xz+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}z+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate $\\frac{∂g}{∂y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int 0\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)={x}^{2}z+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂z}={x}^{2}+{h}^{′}(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}={x}^{2}$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & ={x}^{2}+{h}^{′}(z) \\\\ {h}^{′}(z) & =0 \\\\ h(z) & =C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)={x}^{2}z+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+C.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-124729/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90458c6e-3d72-5235-a1c0-627fe4fd2855"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124729"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81752/selection/dc300a1dfebd87e4f4492246b573ed195ece41100074aed92a6a62dc474c7677" :answer/id #uuid "30b75dc4-720c-595b-bece-ddd1588825b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=y{e}^{xz}+yz+x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81752/selection/ea205e4cdd8c7c23a66864ed881dd8f82e1dcf792255d2e845bdc875d4b3db1e" :answer/id #uuid "953fe1b1-ed35-5b3e-8dff-5c45c750ebfd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=y{e}^{xz}+xy+z+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81752/selection/2fe21ddf9027aa1e97608cd17f478f34fcce10dbaf2ee2001eb4299feae1f9b5" :answer/id #uuid "964af72f-b676-50cb-a55a-19d5d6e8ff9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=y{e}^{xz}+xz+y+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81752/selection/d52711bdee821b72df8ed1c588a1a9e02419035eb1ad0be87e7d9aa9278b0f43" :answer/id #uuid "54274358-8485-5c02-ab59-42969fe59b83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xz{e}^{xz}+xz+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81752/selection/db309b8fb44d2aafec47837cf27f00a1dc257e88648e53362b8964d1842a9ba2" :answer/id #uuid "98426a6a-b390-5371-a75d-26ccfda54f11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xz{e}^{xz}+y+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81752/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ed97c327-c844-5283-a902-987d546686cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81752/selection/2fe21ddf9027aa1e97608cd17f478f34fcce10dbaf2ee2001eb4299feae1f9b5" :answer-field/choices ["q-81752/selection/dc300a1dfebd87e4f4492246b573ed195ece41100074aed92a6a62dc474c7677" "q-81752/selection/ea205e4cdd8c7c23a66864ed881dd8f82e1dcf792255d2e845bdc875d4b3db1e" "q-81752/selection/2fe21ddf9027aa1e97608cd17f478f34fcce10dbaf2ee2001eb4299feae1f9b5" "q-81752/selection/d52711bdee821b72df8ed1c588a1a9e02419035eb1ad0be87e7d9aa9278b0f43" "q-81752/selection/db309b8fb44d2aafec47837cf27f00a1dc257e88648e53362b8964d1842a9ba2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81752" :question/id #uuid "0a7115a4-2aa4-5459-8a09-d018d71ebb7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-81752" :question/problem "Consider the function\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=(yz{e}^{xz}+z)\\,i+({e}^{xz}+1)\\,j+(xy{e}^{xz}+x)\\,k.\n$$\n\nFind $f(x,y,z)$ such that $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z).$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y,z)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{i}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,\\text{j}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\,\\text{k}.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=yz{e}^{xz}+z,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={e}^{xz}+1,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=xy{e}^{xz}+x\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (yz{e}^{xz}+z)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =y{e}^{xz}+xz+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={e}^{xz}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={e}^{xz}+1$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{xz}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & ={e}^{xz}+1 \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we integrate $\\frac{∂g}{∂y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int 1\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =y+h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=y+h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=y{e}^{xz}+xz+y+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=xy{e}^{xz}+x+{h}^{′}(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=xy{e}^{xz}+x$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}xy{e}^{xz}+x+{h}^{′}(z) & =zy{e}^{xz}+x \\\\ {h}^{′}(z) & =0 \\\\ h(z) & =C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=y{e}^{xz}+xz+y+C.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-81752/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90458c6e-3d72-5235-a1c0-627fe4fd2855"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81752"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132100/selection/e6e501395c3d6955651c899fe02f65ef43e8349f06ec7b38a0bf163e840bf5de" :answer/id #uuid "9ae826d7-8fcf-5c70-b83d-2d70b0c01c30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xy\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+xz-{z}^{2}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132100/selection/13c095022b79712258d6c58ebeee2d9c05dd09bddff6aa6d6a449af65b7760b5" :answer/id #uuid "4b41ae6d-98bd-51a9-9c2f-271870196954" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+xy-y{z}^{2}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132100/selection/d9c4f93bce332649fcc2b9e027a5872b38d7bb1ada4e933aebd5766afb785872" :answer/id #uuid "b350f570-eaf2-56ce-976b-b011782ab1d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+x-y{z}^{2}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132100/selection/f88c02daec7220ff30da69dcdf62cd3d59561a6c8d808cb345edcc6f8fcf40fe" :answer/id #uuid "52e34c9c-7538-5dc9-933f-ab262305cdab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+xy+x{z}^{2}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132100/selection/359ee12247751354ea360f6c075b6f74ddfa0795cd08be36a6c98041908f7cc6" :answer/id #uuid "0c6f18bb-929a-54f3-97cd-f4ff7cfa5162" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xz\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+{x}^{2}-y{z}^{2}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132100/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2b9c286f-8698-5499-b7ec-095a4724d1b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132100/selection/d9c4f93bce332649fcc2b9e027a5872b38d7bb1ada4e933aebd5766afb785872" :answer-field/choices ["q-132100/selection/e6e501395c3d6955651c899fe02f65ef43e8349f06ec7b38a0bf163e840bf5de" "q-132100/selection/13c095022b79712258d6c58ebeee2d9c05dd09bddff6aa6d6a449af65b7760b5" "q-132100/selection/d9c4f93bce332649fcc2b9e027a5872b38d7bb1ada4e933aebd5766afb785872" "q-132100/selection/f88c02daec7220ff30da69dcdf62cd3d59561a6c8d808cb345edcc6f8fcf40fe" "q-132100/selection/359ee12247751354ea360f6c075b6f74ddfa0795cd08be36a6c98041908f7cc6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132100" :question/id #uuid "a7a7eb06-4c1e-5068-b4cc-6719124b8cde" :question/math-academy-id "q-132100" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ where $F(x,y,z)=(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+1)\\,i+(\\frac{x}{y}-{z}^{2})\\,j-2yz\\,k.$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y,z)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\,k.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+1,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{x}{y}-{z}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=-2yz\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+x+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{x}{y}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{x}{y}-{z}^{2}$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{y}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{x}{y}-{z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =-{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate $\\frac{∂g}{∂y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int (-{z}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-y{z}^{2}+h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=-y{z}^{2}+h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+x-y{z}^{2}+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=-2yz+{h}^{′}(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=-2yz$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2yz & =-2yz+{h}^{′}(z) \\\\ {h}^{′}(z) & =0 \\\\ h(z) & =C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+x-y{z}^{2}+C.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-132100/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90458c6e-3d72-5235-a1c0-627fe4fd2855"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132100"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81751/selection/27ccedee13607f34a31d1016246000c7d0588c4325a9471e7e4ac8e00887daf2" :answer/id #uuid "80a6ebc7-aa32-5a8a-a8d4-45fc0beb55bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xyz+yz-z+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81751/selection/90cde69bd76fb34862afe928f14b8079192a4744759be42c258dedbadfd4d380" :answer/id #uuid "a5042b49-1563-5ef9-9b26-8d3af6400ee8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2xyz+yz-2+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81751/selection/fe2a8b1f7b61eabba7e3a2a44d4094f44c0558e772737f1ff9f46bc429f929fd" :answer/id #uuid "0c8b54cd-3f4f-5db9-99d7-bccd7c014b1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xy{z}^{2}+yz-2z+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81751/selection/a834e9c133e9c87a288d2ad3ac6ed8d465b4823c1827b616a0f97ba09f42d079" :answer/id #uuid "ff094b55-00d2-530e-8054-a9182524e92f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2xyz+y-2+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81751/selection/bb3eebbfd6db13e1dbfb28b1b446922c18afd97c31b70d432640f949048ce3b2" :answer/id #uuid "efea1b1c-f1af-5b72-b867-590a24735f21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2xy{z}^{2}+y-z+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81751/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fbda860e-4806-5f5a-9f6f-6d521c111004" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81751/selection/fe2a8b1f7b61eabba7e3a2a44d4094f44c0558e772737f1ff9f46bc429f929fd" :answer-field/choices ["q-81751/selection/27ccedee13607f34a31d1016246000c7d0588c4325a9471e7e4ac8e00887daf2" "q-81751/selection/90cde69bd76fb34862afe928f14b8079192a4744759be42c258dedbadfd4d380" "q-81751/selection/fe2a8b1f7b61eabba7e3a2a44d4094f44c0558e772737f1ff9f46bc429f929fd" "q-81751/selection/a834e9c133e9c87a288d2ad3ac6ed8d465b4823c1827b616a0f97ba09f42d079" "q-81751/selection/bb3eebbfd6db13e1dbfb28b1b446922c18afd97c31b70d432640f949048ce3b2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81751" :question/id #uuid "d899f9a7-7e79-55ee-a661-39f0a16b8360" :question/math-academy-id "q-81751" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ where $F(x,y,z)=y{z}^{2}\\,i+(x{z}^{2}+z)\\,j+(2xyz+y-2)\\,k.$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y,z)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\,k.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=y{z}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{z}^{2}+z,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=2xyz+y-2\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int y{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =xy{z}^{2}+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{z}^{2}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{z}^{2}+z$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x{z}^{2}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =x{z}^{2}+z \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate $\\frac{∂g}{∂y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =yz+h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=yz+h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=xy{z}^{2}+yz+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=2xyz+y+{h}^{′}(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=2xyz+y-2$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2xyz+y-2 & =2xyz+y+{h}^{′}(z) \\\\ {h}^{′}(z) & =-2 \\\\ h(z) & =-2z+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=xy{z}^{2}+yz-2z+C.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-81751/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90458c6e-3d72-5235-a1c0-627fe4fd2855"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81751"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132103/selection/d4659ed4e99e726b0d78008cf107acaa300335c523e753539deb6e03cdf2f5aa" :answer/id #uuid "2c09f9e7-5ac8-5afb-9d77-1c8b64e22b10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xy{e}^{z}+{x}^{2}+x+{y}^{2}z+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132103/selection/961a65f5e15f5972c48610e2902ed4a232ee25db7e214d40cdf8be64ef619b78" :answer/id #uuid "26afae2b-4967-5c67-b698-aed2337c915b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xyz{e}^{z}+x+y-{z}^{2}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132103/selection/5a3438b2aa320fbda1f579379ff4dc95a93119240658d7c4b06d6427d48ea966" :answer/id #uuid "b52fd5cc-1063-5b2c-93d2-9cc207cb0604" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xy{e}^{z}+{x}^{2}+y-{z}^{2}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132103/selection/efa02d974ec8a1101d12e1f3a3ee7317287ea5d411706828f19c1f6ade6a003f" :answer/id #uuid "8acbe07f-e3b3-5e7d-8382-067e5d6e7067" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=x{e}^{z}+y{x}^{2}+x-{z}^{2}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132103/selection/adf1f85d70ed469d4197d9739154f3251d82e48121e66eeb7c593bcc5adab4cc" :answer/id #uuid "305c8b43-b597-50fd-877f-54e779c22efb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xy{e}^{z}+x+y-z+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132103/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0d8b2699-b722-565a-a592-e29d42931852" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132103/selection/5a3438b2aa320fbda1f579379ff4dc95a93119240658d7c4b06d6427d48ea966" :answer-field/choices ["q-132103/selection/d4659ed4e99e726b0d78008cf107acaa300335c523e753539deb6e03cdf2f5aa" "q-132103/selection/961a65f5e15f5972c48610e2902ed4a232ee25db7e214d40cdf8be64ef619b78" "q-132103/selection/5a3438b2aa320fbda1f579379ff4dc95a93119240658d7c4b06d6427d48ea966" "q-132103/selection/efa02d974ec8a1101d12e1f3a3ee7317287ea5d411706828f19c1f6ade6a003f" "q-132103/selection/adf1f85d70ed469d4197d9739154f3251d82e48121e66eeb7c593bcc5adab4cc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132103" :question/id #uuid "e741ce65-3525-5109-95f5-b3e26052f7c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-132103" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ where $F(x,y,z)=(2x+y{e}^{z})\\,i+(x{e}^{z}+1)\\,j+(xy{e}^{z}-2z)\\,k.$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y,z)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\,k.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x+y{e}^{z},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{z}+1,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=xy{e}^{z}-2z\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2x+y{e}^{z})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+xy{e}^{z}+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{z}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{z}+1$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x{e}^{z}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =x{e}^{z}+1 \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate $\\frac{∂g}{∂y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int \\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =y+h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=y+h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+xy{e}^{z}+y+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=xy{e}^{z}+{h}^{′}(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=xy{e}^{z}-2z$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}xy{e}^{z}-2z & =xy{e}^{z}+{h}^{′}(z) \\\\ {h}^{′}(z) & =-2z \\\\ h(z) & =-{z}^{2}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=xy{e}^{z}+{x}^{2}+y-{z}^{2}+C.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-132103/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90458c6e-3d72-5235-a1c0-627fe4fd2855"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132103"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7020"] :question/problem "Find $f(x,y)$ such that $\\nabla f = \\mathbf{F},$ where $\\mathbf F(x,y) = 2xy\\ \\mathbf i + (x^2 - 3)\\ \\mathbf j .$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y) = \\dfrac{\\partial{f}}{\\partial{x}}\\,\\textbf{i} + \\dfrac{\\partial{f}}{\\partial{y}}\\,\\textbf{j}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\nabla f(x,y) = \\mathbf F(x,y),$ the function $f(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial{f}}{\\partial{x}} = 2xy, \\qquad \\dfrac{\\partial{f}}{\\partial{y}} = x^2-3.\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\dfrac{\\partial{f}}{\\partial{x}}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 2xy\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}y+g(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial{f}}{\\partial{y}} = x^2 + g'(y).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\dfrac{\\partial{f}}{\\partial{y}} = x^2 -3$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{g}^{′}(y) & ={x}^{2}-3 \\\\ {g}^{′}(y) & =-3 \\\\ g(y) & =-3y+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nFinally, substituting $g(y)=-3y +C$ into our expression for $f(x,y),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y) = x^2y -3y + C.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7184"] :question/problem "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that $\\nabla f(x,y,z)  = \\mathbf{F}(x,y,z),$ where $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z) = yz\\,\\mathbf{i} + (xz + 4z^2)\\,\\mathbf{j} + (xy+8yz)\\,\\mathbf{k}.$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y,z) = \\dfrac{\\partial{f}}{\\partial{x}} \\, \\mathbf{i} + \\dfrac{\\partial{f}}{\\partial{y}} \\, \\mathbf{j} + \\dfrac{\\partial{f}}{\\partial{z}} \\, \\mathbf{k}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\nabla f(x,y,z)  = \\mathbf{F}(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial{f}}{\\partial{x}} = yz, \\qquad \\dfrac{\\partial{f}}{\\partial{y}} = xz + 4z^2, \\qquad \\dfrac{\\partial{f}}{\\partial{z}} = xy+8yz.\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\dfrac{\\partial{f}}{\\partial{x}}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int yz\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =xyz+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial{f}}{\\partial{y}} = xz + \\dfrac{\\partial{g}}{\\partial{y}}.\n$$\n\nTaking $\\dfrac{\\partial{f}}{\\partial{y}} = xz + 4z^2$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}xz+\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =xz+4{z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =4{z}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate $\\dfrac{\\partial{g}}{\\partial{y}}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int 4{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4y{z}^{2}+h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z) = 4yz^2 + h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x, y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z) = xyz + 4yz^2 + h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial{f}}{\\partial{z}} = xy + 8yz + h'(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\dfrac{\\partial{f}}{\\partial{z}} = xy+8yz$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}xy+8yz & =xy+8yz+{h}^{′}(z) \\\\ {h}^{′}(z) & =0 \\\\ h(z) & =C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z) = xyz + 4yz^2 + C.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
